#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Log foods to Cronometer from the terminal.

Cronometer has no public API for personal accounts. Its web app talks to the
server over GWT-RPC, so this tool logs in the way the website does and sends
the same "add food" request the website sends. A saved food is that request,
built when the food was found with crono search and filled in with the date,
meal, and session each time it is logged.

The login flow, build hash lookup, and the authenticate and removeServing
payloads follow github.com/cphoskins/cronometer-mcp (MIT license).
"""

